# Google OAuth Scope Setup Instructions

The code for extracting phone numbers and handling Google OAuth profile syncing is now live in the backend! 

However, because Clerk manages the OAuth flow, you **must** manually configure Clerk and Google Cloud to request the `Calendar` and `Phone Number` permissions from the user. You cannot do this in code; it has to be configured in their dashboards.

Please follow these exact steps to complete the setup:

## 1. Google Cloud Console Configuration

Before Clerk can request these permissions, your Google Cloud OAuth app must be allowed to ask for them.

1. Go to the [Google Cloud Console](https://console.cloud.google.com/).
2. Select the project you use for Soouls authentication.
3. Go to **APIs & Services** > **Library**.
   - Search for **Google People API** and click **Enable**.
   - Search for **Google Calendar API** and click **Enable**.
4. Go to **APIs & Services** > **OAuth consent screen**.
5. Click **Edit App** and navigate to the **Scopes** step.
6. Click **Add or Remove Scopes**.
7. Manually paste the following two scopes into the input field at the bottom of the drawer and click Add:
   - `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/user.phonenumbers.read`
   - `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.events`
8. Save and continue.

> [!WARNING]  
> Because Calendar access is a **Sensitive Scope**, Google will require you to submit your app for verification before you can remove the "Unverified App" warning for your users.

## 2. Clerk Dashboard Configuration

Now that Google allows these scopes, you need to tell Clerk to request them when a user clicks "Sign in with Google".

1. Go to your [Clerk Dashboard](https://dashboard.clerk.com/).
2. Navigate to **User & Authentication** > **Social Connections**.
3. Click the gear icon (Settings) next to **Google**.
4. Scroll down to the **Custom Scopes** section.
5. Add the following two scopes, exactly as written (usually space-separated or comma-separated depending on the Clerk UI):
   - `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/user.phonenumbers.read`
   - `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.events`
6. Click **Save**.

## What happens next?

Once you complete these steps:
1. When a user clicks "Sign up with Google", they will be prompted to grant access to their Calendar and their Phone Number.
2. After they agree and return to Soouls, the backend's `UsersService` will automatically trigger the `GoogleIntegrationService` to grab their Google token from Clerk.
3. The service will fetch their phone number via the Google People API and save it to the database (`users.phoneNumber`), opting them into WhatsApp notifications automatically.
4. (Optional) You can now use the `GoogleIntegrationService` to manage their calendar events by passing their Clerk ID!
